From a4687b681bddb731d1f43abca2b135066d93a663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:01:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the switcher with the theme and make activity a menu
 page

The switcher takes its look from elements of the theme's screen view (switcher*): the
decoration, the texts it fills, the area of the picture with the theme's corners, and the
pager's dots. Pixel art grows by whole steps, and a save's screenshot is used only when it
was taken with that save. Activity is now a page of the themed menu. The job console keeps
its terminal, without spaced letters or scan lines, and sizes its small text from the screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
